# Per-path token ceilings, gated by `itok check` on every commit.
#
# Counts are TOKENIZER-backed (o200k, itok's pinned `--bpe` tier), never a
# bytes/4 heuristic and never a model's guess. That is what makes a ceiling
# comparable across machines and across days -- an estimator that varies per
# run cannot gate anything. rekall does not implement the counter: itok owns
# token accounting and this file is read by itok's own runner (SPEC.md V8).
#
# WHAT THIS CEILING IS: a cap on ENTRY COST. SPEC.md is what an agent loads
# before it does any work in this repo, and that cost is re-billed on every
# turn, so it is subtracted from headroom before anything useful happens. It
# is not a fit constraint -- 6,773 tokens fits any window in use.
#
# It forces a REVIEW, not a shrink. The slack below is deliberate (~13%): a
# ceiling set a hair above the current figure turns every legitimate addition
# into a raise, and a threshold raised reflexively trains the reflex instead
# of catching the problem. When a raise is genuinely right, it belongs in a
# commit that says why -- which is the whole reason the number lives in a
# tracked file rather than in a flag.
#
